    <briefdescription>
<para>Exact IEEE equality, spelled without == so gfortran&apos;s -Wcompare-reals stays quiet at deliberate exact comparisons (sentinels, literal zeros). </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>(a &lt;= b .and. a &gt;= b) is precisely a == b: false for NaN, true for equal infinities and for +0/-0. Not a tolerance test; see <computeroutput>rae</computeroutput> for that. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
